# Vacation Budget App - Cursor AI Rules

## Design Principles
- Follow clean, modern design inspired by Uniswap's aesthetic
- Use established color scheme: primaryPink (#FF3399), secondaryPink (#FF66E6), lightPink (#FF99F2)
- Maintain consistent spacing: 40px for header top padding, 16px for standard padding
- Ensure 44pt minimum touch targets for all interactive elements
- Support both light and dark mode consistently

## SwiftUI Standards
- Follow Apple's Human Interface Guidelines
- Use proper state management with @State, @Published, @EnvironmentObject
- Implement proper error handling and validation
- Use formatCurrency() helper for all monetary displays
- Show decimals only when fractional parts exist

## Number Pad Behavior
- Allow decimal input up to 2 places maximum
- Handle empty field decimal entry (add "0." prefix)
- Use 70x70 circular buttons with proper spacing

## Calendar Functionality
- Toggle represents date presence, not calendar visibility
- Sequential date selection: start → end → complete
- "Done" button explicitly closes calendar
- Pink date display allows re-editing

## Code Quality
- Test all changes thoroughly before implementation
- Provide clear explanations for design decisions
- Maintain existing functionality unless explicitly requested to change
- Use consistent naming conventions and structure
